1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,173
What if I told you winning the toss barely improves your chances of winning an IPL match?

2
00:00:06,343 --> 00:00:07,446
Seriously.

3
00:00:07,576 --> 00:00:09,147
Let's look at the numbers.

4
00:00:09,897 --> 00:00:15,834
Across thousands of matches, toss winners won 54.3% of decided Tests.

5
00:00:15,984 --> 00:00:19,476
But in ODIs, just 49.6%.

6
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:22,556
T20 internationals? 50.3%.

7
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:25,419
And the IPL? 51.6%.

8
00:00:26,569 --> 00:00:28,662
Now imagine you're the captain.

9
00:00:28,792 --> 00:00:31,218
It's an IPL match under lights.

10
00:00:31,328 --> 00:00:33,499
Dew might arrive later.

11
00:00:33,448 --> 00:00:35,211
You've just won the toss.

12
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:36,871
What would you choose?

13
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:39,186
Bat first, or bowl first?

14
00:00:41,886 --> 00:00:47,383
In the IPL data, toss winners choosing to bowl first won nearly 55%.

15
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:51,000
Those choosing to bat won only 45%.

16
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:54,103
But does that mean bowling first always works?

17
00:00:54,353 --> 00:00:55,867
Not necessarily.

18
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:00,733
And here's something even stranger.

19
00:01:00,903 --> 00:01:06,763
In 2024, IPL toss winners won only about 44% of matches.

20
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:10,400
In 2025, that jumped to 61%.

21
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:11,839
Same coin.

22
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:14,065
Completely different results.

23
00:01:15,865 --> 00:01:17,765
Now comes the real twist.

24
00:01:18,015 --> 00:01:24,143
Research found almost no average toss advantage in daytime international limited-overs cricket.

25
00:01:24,443 --> 00:01:30,484
But in day-night matches, that estimated advantage increased to 3.3 percentage points.

26
00:01:31,984 --> 00:01:38,327
In Tests, the estimated toss advantage was even larger, at 4.9 percentage points.

27
00:01:38,577 --> 00:01:44,998
Over five days, the pitch can wear down, cracks can develop, and batting conditions can change dramatically.

28
00:01:46,048 --> 00:01:48,912
So winning the toss isn't a magic formula.

29
00:01:49,082 --> 00:01:51,639
Its value changes with the conditions.

30
00:01:51,839 --> 00:01:56,537
The pitch, the weather, the match format, and the captain's decision all play a part.

31
00:01:58,237 --> 00:02:00,670
So, does winning the toss win matches?

32
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,758
Usually, not by much.

33
00:02:03,008 --> 00:02:07,887
But under the right conditions, that small coin can offer a meaningful advantage.

34
00:02:08,237 --> 00:02:10,045
The toss starts the match.

35
00:02:10,245 --> 00:02:12,213
It doesn't decide the winner.

36
00:02:12,713 --> 00:02:14,428
Beyond The Scoreboard.
